---
import MarkdownLayout from '../../layouts/MarkdownLayout.astro';

const frontmatter = {
	container: '/arkhamrevived/',
	page: 'arkhamrevived',
	title: 'Arkham: Revived - PlayStation 3 Tutorial',
	description: 'Patch Batman: Arkham Origins on PlayStation 3 for Arkham: Revived. Works on OFW backup archives and CFW/HEN consoles.',
};
---
<MarkdownLayout frontmatter={frontmatter}>
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="/arkhamrevived/ps3-tutorial/app/ui.css" />
	<a href="/arkhamrevived/" class="back-link">Back to Arkham: Revived</a>

	<p>
		This page patches <strong>Batman: Arkham Origins</strong> on PlayStation 3 so it connects to
		Arkham: Revived Redux. The tool runs entirely in your browser, which means no downloads or uploads!
	</p>

	<!-- coming soon!
	<p>
		Follow this video guide for help patching Batman: Arkham Origins and connecting to
		Arkham: Revived Redux:
	</p>

	<div style="position: relative; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;">
		<iframe
			src=""
			title="Arkham: Revived PlayStation 3 Tutorial"
			style="position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;"
			allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
			referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
			allowfullscreen
		></iframe>
	</div>

	<br />
	<br />
	-->

	<div id="arkham-patcher">
		<p class="ak-busy">Loading the patcher, this may take a while so please wait...<br>(If it doesn't load, try a different browser like Chrome or Edge)</p>
		<noscript>
			<p class="ak-error-text">This tool needs JavaScript. Enable it and reload the page.</p>
		</noscript>
	</div>

	<h3>Join the Community</h3>
	<p>
		Need help getting connected, troubleshooting an issue, or finding other players?<br/><br/>Join the Arkham: Revived Redux Discord community for support and matchmaking:
	</p>
	<p>
		<a href="https://discord.gg/7BneAcgvZh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Join the Arkham: Revived Discord">
			<img src="/img/discord.png" alt="Join the Arkham: Revived Discord" style="height: 40px; vertical-align: middle;" />
		</a>
		<br/>
		<br/>
	</p>

	<h3>Support Development</h3>
	<p>
		If you enjoy Arkham: Revived Redux and would like to support its development, consider
		donating to my Ko-fi page. I'd really appreciate it!
	</p>

	<div id="kofi-widget-container">
		{/* crossorigin lets the widget load inside the cross-origin isolated page (COEP) */}
		<script type='text/javascript' crossorigin='anonymous' src='https://storage.ko-fi.com/cdn/widget/Widget_2.js'></script>
		<script type='text/javascript'>
			kofiwidget2.init('Support me on Ko-fi', '#72a4f2', 'D1D01P21FF');
			kofiwidget2.draw();
		</script>
	</div>

	<br/>

	<h3>Source Code</h3>
	<p>
		Arkham: Revived and its patching tools are built with open-source projects.
		<br/><br/>
		Explore the repositories below to see how everything works:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<a href="https://github.com/KiwifruitDev/ArkhamRevivedWorker" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ArkhamRevivedWorker</a>: Cloudflare Worker running the Arkham: Revived Redux server.
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="https://github.com/KiwifruitDev/arkham-patcher" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">arkham-patcher</a>: Source code for this browser-based PS3 backup patcher.
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="https://github.com/KiwifruitDev/ps3xport-wasm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ps3xport-wasm</a>: WebAssembly port of ps3xport used by the browser patcher.
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="https://github.com/kakaroto/ps3xport" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ps3xport</a>: Original PS3 backup utility that the WebAssembly port is based on.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<script is:inline type="module" src="/arkhamrevived/ps3-tutorial/app/app.js"></script>
</MarkdownLayout>
